    "selectCount": 2,
    "explanation_en": "Chain of custody is the process of documenting and preserving the integrity of evidence collected during an\nincident response. It involves recording the details of each person who handled the evidence, the time and\ndate of each transfer, and the location where the evidence was stored. Chain of custody ensures that the\nevidence is admissible in legal proceedings and can be traced back to its source. E-discovery, legal hold, and\npreservation are related concepts, but they do not ensure evidence is properly handled. References: CompTIA\nSecurity+ Study Guide: Exam SY0-701, 9th Edition, page 487; NIST SP 800-61: 3.2. Evidence Gathering and\nHandling",
